# class: circulation-privacy
# origin: audits/2026-10-18-first-contact.md S1 (first-contact-plans/3-studio.arch d_bath opens onto the
#   living/kitchen/dining room); README PS2.6. Decided 2026-10-19 (coordinator, review round 1 of PR #203,
#   S1 revision): a kitchen that is also the living room counts where a kitchen fixture stands nearer the
#   bath door than wetDoorKitchenProximityMm (1500). This case is the stronger variant, with the kitchen
#   run beside the door: the audit's own instance has its nearest kitchen fixture 2025 mm from the door,
#   beyond the 1500 mm default, and is silent; there a bath door onto a combined room is a taste question
#   (research/design-taste.md R2), not a warning
# expect: W_WET_ROOM_DOOR
# status: done
# fact: the bathroom's only door, d_bath (x 4100-4900 on w_h, face y 2950 on the living side), opens onto
#   "Living / Kitchen" (uses living kitchen dining) 400 mm from its kitchen_sink (x 2900-3700) and 1300 mm
#   from its stove (x 2200-2800), both against w_h; measured from the doorway's face
plan "Bathroom opening onto the open-plan living room" {
  units mm
  grid 50
  wall id=shell exterior thickness 200 { (0,0) (6000,0) (6000,5000) (0,5000) close }
  wall id=w_h partition thickness 100 { (0,3000) (6000,3000) }
  wall id=w_v partition thickness 100 { (3000,3000) (3000,5000) }
  room id=r_main at (0,0) size 6000x3000 label "Living / Kitchen" uses living kitchen dining
  room id=r_entry at (0,3000) size 3000x2000 label "Entrance" uses entry
  room id=r_bath at (3000,3000) size 3000x2000 label "Bathroom" uses bath
  door id=d_front at (1500,5000) width 900 wall shell swing into r_entry
  opening id=o_entry at (1500,3000) width 900 wall w_h
  door id=d_bath at (4500,3000) width 800 wall w_h swing into r_bath
  window at (3000,0) width 2400 wall shell
  furniture kitchen_sink against wall w_h offset 3300 in r_main
  furniture stove against wall w_h offset 2500 in r_main
  furniture table at (3600,600) size 1600x900
  furniture shower against wall shell segment 1 offset 4450 in r_bath
  furniture wc against wall shell segment 2 offset 1700 in r_bath
  furniture basin against wall shell segment 2 offset 2500 in r_bath
}
